From 74648acf3a80aaa518c61c5a559820f7ae2c117e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(helper): auth --keep-looking: frames without a face use
 up no try

Biopass counts every attempt against `retries`, whether it compared a
face or saw none, so a scan is over after a few seconds of nobody in
front of the camera, and a caller cannot tell "no face" from "a face
that did not match".

FaceAuth now returns NoFace (new AuthResult) when an attempt compared no
face: none found, too small or cut off (min_face_height), a capture or
camera open that failed, or in both-cameras mode a second camera that
saw no face, saw it too late or did not open. Retry stays for a face
that did not match. Without the new option AuthManager treats NoFace as
Retry, so nothing changes.

`biopass-helper auth --keep-looking <ms>` (AuthConfig.keep_looking_ms):
NoFace attempts use up no try; the method keeps looking, retry_delay
apart, for up to <ms> (within the time budget). The first attempt that
compared a face decides: a match is exit 0, a mismatch or an
anti-spoofing failure exit 1 (no retry). Nothing compared: the new exit
3 (HelperExit::NoFace). For callers that count failed faces themselves
and want "nobody there" not to count; the PAM module never passes it
and maps 3, like any unknown code, to PAM_AUTH_ERR.
Tests: auth_manager, helper_exit, face_both_cameras, face_camera_reuse.
